From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 12:36:26 +0200
Subject: net: lantiq: cbm: fail the port-resource lookup when its allocation
 fails

dp_port_resources_get() hands the caller back two things:
*num_tmu_ports, and a kmalloc'd cbm_tmu_res_t array through *res_pp. It
writes the count first, then allocates. If the allocation fails it logs
"error in allocating memory" and falls out of the if/else chain into the
trailing "return 0" -- so the caller is told the lookup succeeded, reads
a count it can believe, and dereferences a *res_pp the function never
wrote. The caller's pointer is whatever it was before the call.

That is the shape we transcribed, because it is what AVM's 07.30 GPL
release does (cbm.c:767-768 in Linux 4.9.198). AVM's 08.25 GPL release
adds the return (cbm.c:791 in Linux 4.9.337), and it is plainly right:
every other exit from this function that cannot produce a result already
says -1, at the *num_tmu_ports bounds check, at the
accel/directpath/checksum arm, at the static-pmac gate and at the
unallocated-pmac tail. The OOM arm was the one that did not.

08.25 adds a second return -1 in the static-pmac LAN/WAN branch, on the
kmalloc there. That branch does not exist here -- it is gated off until
conf_dqm_dma_port is ported -- so there is nothing to take.

Nothing in tree calls cbm_dp_port_resources_get() today; the wrapper is
exported for the consumers that arrive with the rest of the datapath. Which
is the argument for fixing it now rather than after one of them exists.

The provenance comments on the function and at the top of the file said
the body was AVM 07.30 verbatim apart from that gate. That is no longer
true, so both now name this as the second deviation and say which
release it comes from.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm_ports.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm_ports.c
index 797a8462b0a0..bb3a995c18ba 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm_ports.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm_ports.c
@@ -566,6 +566,7 @@ s32 dp_port_resources_get(
 			}
 		} else {
 			pr_err("cbm: %s error in allocating memory", __func__);
+			return -1;
 		}
 	} else if ((!local_entry) &&
 		   ((flags & DP_F_MPE_ACCEL) ||
